&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we run the world&#39;s largest AI platform. We believe the next breakthroughs will come from models trained on domain-specific enterprise data, not from bigger general-purpose models alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s why we built &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/machine-learning/ai-runtime/&quot;&gt;AI Runtime&lt;/a&gt;, a serverless product that makes GPU training of any size feel simple, so companies can train their own models the way frontier labs do. Customers across industries already use it to train models on governed data, from &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/blog/introducing-ai-runtime-scalable-serverless-nvidia-gpus-databricks-training-and-finetuning&quot;&gt;automotive AI&lt;/a&gt; at Rivian to Merck&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.03485&quot;&gt;TEDDY&lt;/a&gt; foundation models for single-cell biology and drug discovery, all the way to agents like &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/blog/meet-karl-faster-agent-enterprise-knowledge-powered-custom-rl&quot;&gt;KARL&lt;/a&gt; from Databricks AI Research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It takes a lot of engineering to make that work, and we&#39;ve written about it on our blog: how we &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/blog/how-we-keep-gpus-reliable-across-databricks-ai&quot;&gt;keep GPUs reliable&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/blog/fast-fault-tolerant-pytorch-training-ai-runtime&quot;&gt;make training fault-tolerant&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/blog/reducing-qwen-training-time-6x-ai-runtime&quot;&gt;speed up fine-tuning&lt;/a&gt; with fused kernels and smart sequence packing. As a Senior Software Engineer, you&#39;ll work on the systems behind all of this, solving hard technical problems and helping shape how AI Runtime evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build core parts of AI Runtime and contribute to Databricks&#39; technical direction in AI training infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reliability and observability features for a fleet that keeps growing in scale and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve AI Runtime&#39;s developer experience, so the largest training jobs feel as simple as a first experiment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help prepare AI Runtime for new GPU generations and workload types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on hard multi-node training problems, from orchestration and GPU scheduling to data loading and checkpointing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make training faster and cheaper by raising GPU efficiency across model architectures and hardware generations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with research, product, and customers on what we build next and own features from design through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion engineering excellence, raise the bar, and help the engineers around you grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in large-scale distributed systems, with experience in GPU training, high-performance computing, or ML systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training large models with FSDP, DeepSpeed, or Megatron, and familiarity with parallelism strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of GPU performance, including accelerator architecture, high-speed interconnects, and kernels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of training resilience patterns, such as checkpointing, failure detection, and automatic recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in building and running multi-tenant cloud platforms as products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning complex features end to end and seeing them through to customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The clarity to explain technical designs in writing and in person, and a reputation as a teammate others learn from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science or a related field (MS or PhD preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipates utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Local Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$225,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
